the","s":53.499,"e":53.579},{"text":"time.","s":53.739,"e":54.299},{"text":"A","s":54.379,"e":54.459},{"text":"little","s":54.539,"e":54.779},{"text":"overconfident.","s":54.859,"e":55.979}]},{"template":"quote","chapter":"Why chatbots drift","narration":"Why does this need saying at all? Because chat models are famously badly calibrated. Pretrained models are fairly well calibrated, but post-training for chat, as researcher Desi Ivanova puts it, destroys calibration. People like answers that sound sure, so models learn to sound sure.","params":{"text":"Post training… the losses there are not proper scoring rules… *actually destroys calibration*, and this is also very well documented.","who":"Desi Ivanova","role":"researcher, on LLM uncertainty","src":"Estimating and Calibrating Uncertainty in LLMs","t":1175},"start":56.577,"dur":20.281,"words":[{"text":"Why","s":56.877,"e":57.117},{"text":"does","s":57.197,"e":57.357},{"text":"this","s":57.437,"e":57.517},{"text":"need","s":57.637,"e":57.757},{"text":"saying","s":57.837,"e":58.077},{"text":"at","s":58.157,"e":58.237},{"text":"all?","s":58.437,"e":58.877},{"text":"Because","s":59.117,"e":59.357},{"text":"chat","s":59.437,"e":59.677},{"text":"models","s":59.757,"e":60.077},{"text":"are","s":60.157,"e":60.397},{"text":"famously","s":60.477,"e":61.037},{"text":"badly","s":61.197,"e":61.597},{"text":"calibrated.","s":61.717,"e":62.717},{"text":"Pretrained","s":62.837,"e":63.197},{"text":"models","s":63.277,"e":63.597},{"text":"are","s":63.717,"e":63.837},{"text":"fairly","s":63.957,"e":64.237},{"text":"well","s":64.317,"e":64.397},{"text":"calibrated,","s":64.477,"e":65.437},{"text":"but","s":65.557,"e":65.677},{"text":"post-training","s":65.757,"e":66.317},{"text":"for","s":66.397,"e":66.477},{"text":"chat,","s":66.557,"e":67.117},{"text":"as","s":67.237,"e":67.357},{"text":"researcher","s":67.557,"e":67.837},{"text":"Desi","s":67.917,"e":68.157},{"text":"Ivanova","s":68.237,"e":68.717},{"text":"puts","s":68.837,"e":68.957},{"text":"it,","s":69.037,"e":69.437},{"text":"destroys","s":69.637,"e":70.237},{"text":"calibration.","s":70.317,"e":71.597},{"text":"People","s":71.757,"e":71.917},{"text":"like","s":72.037,"e":72.157},{"text":"answers","s":72.357,"e":72.557},{"text":"that","s":72.637,"e":72.717},{"text":"sound","s":72.797,"e":73.037},{"text":"sure,","s":73.197,"e":73.917},{"text":"so","s":74.077,"e":74.237},{"text":"models","s":74.477,"e":74.797},{"text":"learn","s":74.877,"e":75.117},{"text":"to","s":75.197,"e":75.277},{"text":"sound","s":75.397,"e":75.517},{"text":"sure.","s":75.597,"e":76.237}]},{"template":"compare","chapter":"Independent tests","narration":"Independent testers have checked the decision models directly. Ryan Porter ran 3,600 hard reasoning questions through OpenAI's Decisions API and Jev. Luna said ninety nine percent or more on 2,672 answers, and only sixty eight percent of those were right. Jev said ninety nine percent on 1,667 answers, and was right on ninety eight point nine.","params":{"title":"Answers stated at ≥ 99% (3,600 hard questions)","left":{"title":"Decisions API (Luna)","who":"mull","tone":"bad","items":[{"text":"**2,672** answers at ≥ 99%","at":"2,672"},{"text":"**68%** of them right","at":"sixty eight"}]},"right":{"title":"Jev","who":"snap","tone":"good","items":[{"text":"**1,667** answers at ≥ 99%","at":"1,667"},{"text":"**98.9%** of them right","at":"ninety eight point nine"}]},"vs":"vs","hnote":{"text":"Ryan Porter, Anthus, Oct 2026","at":"Ryan Porter","p":[50,77],"pp":[50,76]}},"start":76.858,"dur":27.229,"words":[{"text":"Independent","s":77.158,"e":77.718},{"text":"testers","s":77.878,"e":78.198},{"text":"have","s":78.278,"e":78.438},{"text":"checked","s":78.558,"e":78.678},{"text":"the","s":78.718,"e":78.758},{"text":"decision","s":78.958,"e":79.158},{"text":"models","s":79.238,"e":79.558},{"text":"directly.","s":79.638,"e":80.758},{"text":"Ryan","s":80.838,"e":81.078},{"text":"Porter","s":81.158,"e":81.478},{"text":"ran","s":81.558,"e":81.798},{"text":"3,600","s":81.878,"e":82.038},{"text":"hard","s":82.198,"e":83.238},{"text":"reasoning","s":83.398,"e":84.038},{"text":"questions","s":84.118,"e":84.598},{"text":"through","s":84.678,"e":84.918},{"text":"OpenAI's","s":85.078,"e":85.558},{"text":"Decisions","s":85.638,"e":86.118},{"text":"API","s":86.158,"e":86.758},{"text":"and","s":86.838,"e":86.918},{"text":"Jev.","s":87.078,"e":88.038},{"text":"Luna","s":88.118,"e":88.358},{"text":"said","s":88.438,"e":88.678},{"text":"ninety","s":88.758,"e":88.998},{"text":"nine","s":89.078,"e":89.238},{"text":"percent","s":89.318,"e":89.638},{"text":"or","s":89.718,"e":89.798},{"text":"more","s":89.958,"e":90.278},{"text":"on","s":90.358,"e":90.598},{"text":"2,672","s":90.678,"e":91.158},{"text":"answers,","s":91.318,"e":93.478},{"text":"and","s":93.518,"e":93.558},{"text":"only","s":93.638,"e":93.878},{"text":"sixty","s":93.958,"e":94.358},{"text":"eight","s":94.398,"e":94.438},{"text":"percent","s":94.598,"e":94.838},{"text":"of","s":94.878,"e":94.918},{"text":"those","s":94.998,"e":95.158},{"text":"were","s":95.238,"e":95.318},{"text":"right.","s":95.398,"e":96.278},{"text":"Jev","s":96.358,"e":96.598},{"text":"said","s":96.678,"e":96.918},{"text":"ninety","s":96.998,"e":97.318},{"text":"nine","s":97.398,"e":97.478},{"text":"percent","s":97.558,"e":97.958},{"text":"on","s":98.038,"e":98.198},{"text":"1,667","s":98.278,"e":100.198},{"text":"answers,","s":100.278,"e":101.078},{"text":"and","s":101.118,"e":101.158},{"text":"was","s":101.238,"e":101.398},{"text":"right","s":101.518,"e":101.638},{"text":"on","s":101.718,"e":101.958},{"text":"ninety","s":102.038,"e":102.278},{"text":"eight","s":102.358,"e":102.438},{"text":"point","s":102.518,"e":102.758},{"text":"nine.","s":102.838,"e":103.478}]},{"template":"quote","chapter":"Model by model","narration":"But don't turn that into a rule about paradigms. A team that checked Jev against 2,416 human judgments of police crash reports found it wasn't overconfident there at all. It hedged, staying too close to the middle. Their conclusion is the one to remember: calibration turns out to be a property of the individual model, rather than of the paradigm.","params":{"text":"Calibration turns out to be *a property of the individual model* rather than of the paradigm.","who":"Amir Rafe & Subasish Das","role":"Calibrated Decisions at Scale (arXiv)","src":"police crash narratives with Jev, 2026"},"start":104.087,"dur":24.016,"words":[{"text":"But","s":104.387,"e":104.627},{"text":"don't","s":104.707,"e":104.867},{"text":"turn","s":104.987,"e":105.107},{"text":"that","s":105.187,"e":105.267},{"text":"into","s":105.387,"e":105.507},{"text":"a","s":105.587,"e":105.747},{"text":"rule","s":105.827,"e":106.147},{"text":"about","s":106.307,"e":106.467},{"text":"paradigms.","s":106.587,"e":107.747},{"text":"A","s":107.827,"e":107.907},{"text":"team","s":108.027,"e":108.147},{"text":"that","s":108.227,"e":108.307},{"text":"checked","s":108.427,"e":108.547},{"text":"Jev","s":108.627,"e":108.867},{"text":"against","s":109.067,"e":109.267},{"text":"2,416","s":109.347,"e":111.267},{"text":"human","s":111.427,"e":111.747},{"text":"judgments","s":111.827,"e":112.307},{"text":"of","s":112.387,"e":112.467},{"text":"police","s":112.547,"e":112.787},{"text":"crash","s":112.867,"e":113.107},{"text":"reports","s":113.507,"e":113.907},{"text":"found","s":114.067,"e":114.227},{"text":"it","s":114.307,"e":114.387},{"text":"wasn't","s":114.467,"e":114.707},{"text":"overconfident","s":114.787,"e":115.507},{"text":"there","s":115.587,"e":115.667},{"text":"at","s":115.707,"e":115.747},{"text":"all.","s":115.827,"e":116.547},{"text":"It","s":116.627,"e":116.707},{"text":"hedged,","s":116.787,"e":117.507},{"text":"staying","s":117.547,"e":117.907},{"text":"too","s":117.987,"e":118.147},{"text":"close","s":118.227,"e":118.467},{"text":"to","s":118.507,"e":118.547},{"text":"the","s":118.627,"e":118.707},{"text":"middle.","s":118.867,"e":119.507},{"text":"Their