bration error is the average gap between stated probability and actual accuracy, weighted by how many answers fall in each bin. Zero is perfect. The Brier score is the mean squared error of the probabilities themselves. Always guessing fifty fifty on a yes or no question scores point two five, so you want to be well below that.","params":{"title":"Two numbers to track","parts":[{"text":"ECE","sub":"weighted gap between stated and actual · 0 is perfect","tone":"agent","at":"Expected calibration error"},{"op":"+"},{"text":"Brier","sub":"mean squared error of the probabilities · coin flip = 0.25","tone":"s2","at":"Brier score"}],"caption":"Track both, per question, on a few hundred labeled examples from your own traffic.","caption_at":"well below"},"start":147.966,"dur":25.139,"words":[{"text":"Two","s":148.266,"e":148.506},{"text":"numbers","s":148.586,"e":148.906},{"text":"summarize","s":148.986,"e":149.386},{"text":"it.","s":149.466,"e":149.706},{"text":"Expected","s":150.106,"e":150.586},{"text":"calibration","s":150.666,"e":151.226},{"text":"error","s":151.306,"e":151.626},{"text":"is","s":151.706,"e":151.866},{"text":"the","s":151.986,"e":152.106},{"text":"average","s":152.186,"e":152.506},{"text":"gap","s":152.586,"e":152.826},{"text":"between","s":152.906,"e":153.146},{"text":"stated","s":153.306,"e":153.626},{"text":"probability","s":153.706,"e":154.346},{"text":"and","s":154.426,"e":154.586},{"text":"actual","s":154.746,"e":155.146},{"text":"accuracy,","s":155.226,"e":156.266},{"text":"weighted","s":156.426,"e":156.586},{"text":"by","s":156.666,"e":156.826},{"text":"how","s":156.906,"e":156.986},{"text":"many","s":157.066,"e":157.226},{"text":"answers","s":157.306,"e":157.706},{"text":"fall","s":157.786,"e":157.946},{"text":"in","s":157.986,"e":158.026},{"text":"each","s":158.106,"e":158.266},{"text":"bin.","s":158.426,"e":158.746},{"text":"Zero","s":159.306,"e":159.706},{"text":"is","s":159.866,"e":159.946},{"text":"perfect.","s":160.106,"e":160.666},{"text":"The","s":161.146,"e":161.226},{"text":"Brier","s":161.306,"e":161.626},{"text":"score","s":161.706,"e":162.026},{"text":"is","s":162.106,"e":162.186},{"text":"the","s":162.266,"e":162.346},{"text":"mean","s":162.506,"e":162.666},{"text":"squared","s":162.746,"e":163.146},{"text":"error","s":163.226,"e":163.466},{"text":"of","s":163.546,"e":163.626},{"text":"the","s":163.666,"e":163.706},{"text":"probabilities","s":163.786,"e":164.426},{"text":"themselves.","s":164.466,"e":165.466},{"text":"Always","s":165.706,"e":165.946},{"text":"guessing","s":166.026,"e":166.346},{"text":"fifty","s":166.426,"e":166.666},{"text":"fifty","s":166.826,"e":167.146},{"text":"on","s":167.226,"e":167.306},{"text":"a","s":167.386,"e":167.426},{"text":"yes","s":167.466,"e":167.626},{"text":"or","s":167.706,"e":167.786},{"text":"no","s":167.866,"e":167.946},{"text":"question","s":168.026,"e":168.506},{"text":"scores","s":168.586,"e":168.986},{"text":"point","s":169.146,"e":169.306},{"text":"two","s":169.426,"e":169.546},{"text":"five,","s":169.746,"e":170.266},{"text":"so","s":170.346,"e":170.506},{"text":"you","s":170.666,"e":170.746},{"text":"want","s":170.826,"e":170.906},{"text":"to","s":170.946,"e":170.986},{"text":"be","s":171.066,"e":171.146},{"text":"well","s":171.306,"e":171.546},{"text":"below","s":171.626,"e":171.866},{"text":"that.","s":171.946,"e":172.506}]},{"template":"code","chapter":"Measuring it","narration":"You can measure it in a dozen lines. Bin the answers by stated probability, compare each bin's average probability with its accuracy, and weight the gaps. Run it on a few hundred of your own labeled examples, per question, and again whenever the model version changes.","params":{"file":"calibration.py","lang":"py","lines":["def ece(rows, bins=10):","    # rows: (stated_probability, was_right)","    groups = [[] for _ in range(bins)]","    for p, ok in rows:","        groups[min(int(p * bins), bins - 1)].append((p, ok))","    err = 0.0","    for grp in groups:","        if grp:","            conf = sum(p for p, _ in grp) / len(grp)","            acc = sum(ok for _, ok in grp) / len(grp)","            err += len(grp) / len(rows) * abs(conf - acc)","    return err","","brier = sum((p - ok) ** 2 for p, ok in rows) / len(rows)"],"hl":[{"from":9,"to":11,"label":"stated vs actual, weighted","tone":"agent","at":"compare each bin"}]},"start":173.105,"dur":17.146,"words":[{"text":"You","s":173.405,"e":173.565},{"text":"can","s":173.645,"e":173.725},{"text":"measure","s":173.885,"e":174.045},{"text":"it","s":174.125,"e":174.205},{"text":"in","s":174.245,"e":174.285},{"text":"a","s":174.365,"e":174.525},{"text":"dozen","s":174.565,"e":174.845},{"text":"lines.","s":174.925,"e":175.605},{"text":"Bin","s":175.805,"e":175.965},{"text":"the","s":176.005,"e":176.045},{"text":"answers","s":176.125,"e":176.525},{"text":"by","s":176.605,"e":176.685},{"text":"stated","s":176.765,"e":177.085},{"text":"probability,","s":177.445,"e":178.125},{"text":"compare","s":178.205,"e":178.605},{"text":"each","s":178.725,"e":178.845},{"text":"bin's","s":178.925,"e":179.325},{"text":"average","s":179.485,"e":179.645},{"text":"probability","s":179.725,"e":180.365},{"text":"with","s":180.405,"e":180.445},{"text":"its","s":180.565,"e":180.685},{"text":"accuracy,","s":180.765,"e":181.645},{"text":"and","s":181.725,"e":181.805},{"text":"weight","s":181.925,"e":182.045},{"text":"the","s":182.085,"e":182.125},{"text":"gaps.","s":182.205,"e":183.005},{"text":"Run","s":183.085,"e":183.165},{"text":"it","s":183.245,"e":183.325},{"text":"on","s":183.365,"e":183.405},{"text":"a","s":183.485,"e":183.645},{"text":"few","s":183.725,"e":183.805},{"text":"hundred","s":183.885,"e":184.205},{"text":"of","s":184.285,"e":184.365},{"text":"your","s":184.445,"e":184.525},{"text":"own","s":184.605,"e":184.765},{"text":"labeled","s":184.805,"e":185.085},{"text":"examples,","s":185.405,"e":185.885},{"text":"per","s":185.965,"e":186.045},{"text":"question,","s":186.125,"e":186.925},{"text":"and","s":187.005,"e":187.085},{"text":"again","s":187.285,"e":187.485},{"text":"whenever","s":187.565,"e":187.965},{"text":"the","s":188.045,"e":188.085},{"text":"model","s":188.125,"e":188.365},{"text":"version","s":188.445,"e":188.685},{"text":"changes.","s":188.765,"e":189.645}]},{"template":"statement","chapter":"Fixing it","narration":"And if it's off in a consistent direction, you can fix it cheaply. Fit a tiny logistic regression from the model's probability to what actually happened, called Platt scaling, on held-out labels. The crash narrative team cut calibration error by a factor of three point three this way. One limit: remapping fixes calibration, but it can't add information the probabilities don't carry.","params":{"eyebrow":"Platt scaling: a 2-parameter fix","text":"Recalibration fixes the *numbers*, not the *ranking*.","sub":"Crash-narrative study: ECE 0.0231 → 0.0069 (3.3×) with a few thousand labels.","sub_at":"three point three","art":"tool","tone":"good","punch":"three point three"},"start":190.251,"dur":24.434,"words":[{"text":"And","s":190.551,"e":190.711},{"text":"if","s":190.751,"e":190.791},{"text":"it's","s":190.871,"e":191.031},{"text":"off","s":191.151,"e":191.271},{"text":"in","s":191.311,"e":191.351},{"text":"a","s":191.391,"e":191.431},{"text":"consistent","s":191.511,"e":191.991},{"text":"direction,","s":192.071,"e":192.871},{"text":"you","s":192.911,"e":192.951},{"text":"can","s":193.031,"e":193.111},{"text":"fix","s":193.191,"e":193.351},{"text":"it","s":193.431,"e":193.511},{"text":"cheaply.","s":193.631,"e":194.271},{"text":"Fit","s":194.551,"e":194.711},{"text":"a","s":194.791,"e":194.871},{"text":"tiny","s":195.071,"e":195.271},{"text":"logistic","s":195.391,"e":195.751},{"text":"regression","s":195.831,"e":196.311},{"text":"from","s":196.391,"e":196.551},{"text":"the","s":196.591,"e":196.631},{"text":"model's","s":196.711,"e":197.031},{"text":"probability","s":197.391,"e":197.751},{"text":"to","s":197.791,"e":197.831},{"text"