 80% of the time","It's underconfident","Nothing: calibration is about single answers"],"answer":1,"explain":"400 of 500 is 80%, below the 90% it claimed. Recalibrate, or treat its 0.9 as 0.8 when you set thresholds."},"start":214.685,"dur":13.859,"words":[{"text":"Quick","s":214.985,"e":215.225},{"text":"check.","s":215.305,"e":215.825},{"text":"A","s":216.025,"e":216.105},{"text":"model","s":216.185,"e":216.425},{"text":"gave","s":216.505,"e":216.665},{"text":"probability","s":216.745,"e":217.385},{"text":"point","s":217.545,"e":217.785},{"text":"nine","s":217.945,"e":218.265},{"text":"on","s":218.425,"e":218.665},{"text":"five","s":218.785,"e":218.905},{"text":"hundred","s":218.985,"e":219.225},{"text":"answers,","s":219.505,"e":219.945},{"text":"and","s":220.065,"e":220.185},{"text":"four","s":220.345,"e":220.505},{"text":"hundred","s":220.585,"e":220.825},{"text":"of","s":220.865,"e":220.905},{"text":"them","s":220.985,"e":221.065},{"text":"were","s":221.145,"e":221.305},{"text":"right.","s":221.505,"e":221.945},{"text":"What","s":222.185,"e":222.265},{"text":"does","s":222.345,"e":222.425},{"text":"that","s":222.505,"e":222.585},{"text":"tell","s":222.665,"e":222.825},{"text":"you?","s":222.905,"e":223.385}]},{"template":"exercise","chapter":"Try it","narration":"Try it. Have your agent build a calibration report for one of your decisions.","params":{"title":"Measure your calibration","intro":"Paste this into your coding agent:","prompt":"For one decision we make with a model, collect 200-300 examples with\ntrusted labels from real traffic. Run the model on all of them and log\nthe probability of the chosen answer. Then report: accuracy, a\n10-bin reliability table (stated vs actual), ECE and Brier score.\nFit Platt scaling on half the data and report ECE on the other half,\nbefore and after. Save the script so we can rerun it on every model\nversion change."},"start":228.544,"dur":5.469,"words":[{"text":"Try","s":228.844,"e":229.164},{"text":"it.","s":229.284